@page "/tables/simple-table/rows/drag-and-drop"

@using ViciOne.Ui.Blazor.Components.Tables.Shared.Enums
@using ViciOne.Ui.Blazor.Components.Tables.SimpleTable.Components
@using ViciOne.Ui.Blazor.Components.Tables.SimpleTable.Components.Columns
@using ViciOne.Ui.Blazor.Components.Tables.SimpleTable.Components.Filters

<h3>Draggable Rows</h3>

<DescriptionBanner>
    When <code>RowsDraggable</code> is set, rows can be dragged to any registered dropzone.

    Dragging a row that is part of the current selection carries the whole selection;
    dragging an unselected row selects it first, just like a click.

    Select one or more rows, then drag — the dropzone reports how many rows landed.
</DescriptionBanner>

<DescriptionBanner>
    <code>DragPayloadProvider</code> decides what the drag actually carries. Filtering never removes anything
    from <code>SelectedItems</code>, so without one a drag drops selected rows the filter hides — rows the
    user cannot even see on the table it started from. The provider here keeps only what
    <code>VisibleSelectionChanged</code> last reported, so the drag carries what the table shows and nothing
    else.

    Provider and mirror are scoped services rather than page state, so the rule is testable on its own and the
    page holds neither the set nor a handler for it. Scoped means per circuit: the mirror outlives navigating
    away from this page, and two tables sharing one store would overwrite each other.

    Select several rows, filter the Key column so some of them disappear, then drag one of the rows that is
    left: the dropzone counts only those.
</DescriptionBanner>

<p>@_selectedItems.Count selected, @VisibleSelection.Count of them left by the filter.</p>

@* TItem stated explicitly: the callback below is a method group, which carries no type to infer it
   from. *@
<SimpleTable TItem="ExampleTableItem"
             Items="s_items"
             SelectionMode="SelectionMode.Multiple"
             @bind-SelectedItems="_selectedItems"
             VisibleSelectionChanged="VisibleSelection.Store"
             DragPayloadProvider="DragPayloadProvider"
             RowsDraggable="true"
             MaximumHeight="300px">
    <Columns>
        <SimpleTableTemplateColumn Id="Key" Title="Key">
            <CellContent>
                @context.Key
            </CellContent>
            <FilterEditor>
                <SimpleTableContainsColumnFilterEditor ValueSelector="x => x.Key" />
            </FilterEditor>
        </SimpleTableTemplateColumn>
        <SimpleTableTemplateColumn Id="Value" Title="Value">
            <CellContent>
                @context.Value
            </CellContent>
        </SimpleTableTemplateColumn>
        <SimpleTableTemplateColumn Id="Timestamp" Title="Timestamp">
            <CellContent>
                @context.Timestamp
            </CellContent>
        </SimpleTableTemplateColumn>
    </Columns>
</SimpleTable>

<RowDropzone />
